/**
\class pdg::Bone
\brief Animate a single bone in a Sprite's current rig.

Use Sprite::getBone() after enabling the animation pose. Bone inherits Animated
scheduling, scripts, easing, waits, pause, cancellation and completion handlers.
Position and attachment coordinates are parent-relative; rotation is in radians
and time is in seconds. moveTo(), rotateTo() and changeScaleTo() override their channels,
starting from the displayed value. moveBy() and rotateBy() add to each fresh clip
sample. changeScaleBy() adds a scale delta to each fresh clip sample. Completed controls persist.

Height measures bone length and width measures its transverse bounds/capsule.
Resize keeps child attachment positions proportional while preserving child sizes.
Scale and flip propagate through descendants. Imported bone axes are preserved.
Initial dimensions come from child connection distances, with unit length for a
terminal bone; physical bones use their capsule dimensions. centerOffset is the
attachment point in the parent frame; changing it adds a displacement from its
reference position to the running clip's attachment motion.

Controls run before pose modifiers and IK. Final rotations honor explicit limits,
limits on a corresponding named Part, configured two-bone IK limits, and rotary
limits connecting mapped physical Parts. Physical simulation owns dynamic poses;
scripted controls supply animation targets. Resize updates capsule geometry and
joint anchors outside locked solver callbacks. Scaling or reflecting a single
live physical bone requires disabling animation physics first; use resize for
physical dimensions, or Sprite flip to reflect the entire physical assembly.

The Sprite advances controls automatically, including while its clip is paused.
Use pauseSchedule() to pause the controls. Pose queries never advance their clocks.
Replacing or disabling the rig invalidates handles. isAttached() remains safe;
other getters and edits throw after invalidation. Bone handles and their controls
are runtime state and are not included in Sprite snapshots.

\note The Sprite must have an enabled animation pose. Do not edit controls inside
pose modifier callbacks. Use the callback's borrowed pose to edit that pose.

\par Example
\code{.js}
const forearm = sprite.getBone('forearm');
forearm.series()
    .rotateBy(0.5, 0.3, pdg.easeInOutQuad)
    .wait(0.2)
    .diminish(0, 0.25)
    .endSeries();
\endcode

\see Sprite::enableAnimationPose(), Sprite::getBone(), Animated
*/

/**
\fn pdg::Sprite::getBone(string name)
\brief Get animated controls for a bone in the current rig.

\param name Authored bone name; unknown names throw.
\return A retained Bone handle with stable identity in this Sprite and rig.
\note Enable the Sprite's animation pose first. Handles become invalid when
that rig is replaced or disabled.
\see Bone, getAnimationBoneNames()
*/


/**
\fn pdg::Sprite::getBone(uint id)
\brief Get animated controls for a bone in the current rig.

\param id Bone ID in the current rig; unknown IDs throw.
\return A retained Bone handle with stable identity in this Sprite and rig.
\note Enable the Sprite's animation pose first. Handles become invalid when
that rig is replaced or disabled.
\see Bone, getAnimationBoneNames()
*/


/**
\fn pdg::Bone::diminish(number influence, number seconds, int easing)
\brief Ease scripted bone influence back toward the running animation.

Blends controlled channels toward each fresh authored sample. Zero releases all
controlled channels, including flips. This changes scripted influence, not alpha.
A value between zero and one retains the corresponding fraction of control.

\param influence Finite factor from zero to one.
\param seconds Finite nonnegative duration in seconds.
\param easing Easing constant; default pdg.linearTween.
\return This Bone for chaining.
\see getInfluence(), Animated::series()
*/

/**
\fn pdg::Bone::setIKLimits(number minimum, number maximum)
\brief Set final local rotation limits.
\param minimum Finite lower angle in radians.
\param maximum Finite upper angle, no smaller than minimum and at most one turn above it.
\return This Bone for chaining. Invalid ranges throw without changing the limits.
\see clearIKLimits()
*/

/**
\fn pdg::Bone::setIKLimits(PhysicsConstraint constraint)
\brief Share a live rotary limit with the bone.

The constraint must join this bone's physical Part and its physical parent.
Changes to the constraint update limits immediately. Disconnecting it releases
its limit; clearIKLimits() removes the explicit association without disconnecting
physics. Automatically discovered physical or IK limits may still apply.

\param constraint Active rotary limit for this bone's physical joint.
\return This Bone for chaining; incompatible constraints throw.
\see PhysicsConstraint::setAngleLimits(), clearIKLimits()
*/

/**
\fn pdg::Bone::clearIKLimits()
\brief Remove this Bone's explicit limit override.
\return This Bone for chaining. Existing Part, IK and physical-joint limits still apply.
*/
